Agreed, the dispatcher check before loading is the better place. Proposal for=
 the new rule, effective Monday 12 Oct: no loading of dangerous goods without=
 a dispatcher check of the DGD, recorded in a checklist in the WMS. Lukas, ca=
n you build the checklist as a mandatory step in the loading task for ADR del=
iveries? Items I suggest: DGD printed and signed, UN number and quantity matc=
h the delivery, packing group stated, driver ADR certificate valid, written i=
nstructions in the cab. Five items, all must be ticked before the task can be=
 closed.

Best regards,
Marta Kowalska
Customs coordinator
Corp Europe B.V. | Rotterdam
T +31 10 303 7227

